# `eol=lf` and not just `text=auto`: `text=auto` normalizes to LF *in the index*, but the checkout
# still honours `core.autocrlf`, which GitHub's windows-latest runner sets to `true`. So a file the
# generator emits with LF, and the index stores with LF, arrived in the Windows CI working tree with
# CRLF -- and every guard that compares generated bytes to on-disk bytes, or slices source on a
# literal `\n}\n`, failed there and only there. Pinning the checkout ending makes the working tree
# match the index on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.pdf binary
